MID_SE_Tal_Dan_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_C_001: Well! I'd expect nothing less from such a talented\nplaywright. Even promotional work is easy for you.
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_C_002: Thanks to your ingenious sales pitch, our profits have\nnearly doubled!
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_C_003: Hehehe. Well of course, a good pitch is just\nanother kind of story. I'm glad it helped!
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_C_004: You have no idea. As a show of my appreciation,\nI've added this onto your payment.
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_C_005: No need. I didn't you offer my talents in hopes of\ncompensation.
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_C_006: It's rare that I get to write promotional text—I saw it\nas an opportunity to flex that muscle.
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_C_007: So, you believe experience is its own reward, eh?\nHehe. I knew I liked you for a reason.
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_C_008: You know, I may not look it, but I've always been a\nfan of theater. What is it you use to write your plays?
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_C_009: Why, nothing special. I write on paper made from\npulped reeds, using a bird's-feather quill.
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_C_010: I see, I see. And the feathers, they wear quickly and\nmust be replaced often, correct?
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_C_011: Well, then, may I present to you...a very rare writing\ntool I just happen to have on me.
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_C_012: What is this? White cane of some kind... No.\nIs that bone?
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_C_013: It's made from monoceros horn. It's hard, durable,\nand won't wear regardless of how often it's used.
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_C_014: Forged by a master craftsman, the hassle of \nconstantly changing quills is a thing of the past!
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_C_015: But what's a writing utensil without something to\nwrite on, eh? Here. As a bonus.
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_C_016: This is an extremely rare material called parchment.\nSpecial-ordered from across the sea.
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_C_017: Hmph. You think so little of my writing that you\nbelieve I need these implements to aid me?
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_C_018: Why, not at all! I simply thought you might enjoy a\nchange of pace.
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_C_019: An old animal horn and some baked sheepskins.\nMost unusual.
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_C_020: But it's just as well. You gave them to me, so I'll take\nthem and let you know what I think.
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_C_021: Oh? I'm glad you're so eager to give them a try.\nI await your review...
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_C_022: The true auteur rarely shuns new experiences.\nOne never knows what will spur one's next idea.
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_B_001: Talimun. There you are!
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_B_002: Oh, it's you, Dante. For a moment I thought you were\none of the other vendors. What can I do for you?
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_B_003: The parchment and the monoceros horn you\ngave me—they led to the most wonderful outcome!
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_B_004: Hehehe. Just like I said! They made writing\na breeze, didn't they?
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_B_005: Oh no, they were absolutely dreadful. The horn's tip\nwas so sharp, it caught on the pages.
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_B_006: Wha— Really?!
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_B_007: And the parchment itself refused to be rolled up.\nMuch too stiff.
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_B_008: Oh, you have my sincerest apologies. They must have\nbeen defective products...
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_B_009: I'll say, for a dissatisfied customer, you do seem\nrather...cheery?
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_B_010: Well, I was trying to write with my useless tools,\ncursing your name for burdening me with them...
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_B_011: and I saw the inanity of it. At least two animals were\nkilled to make a bad pen and worthless paper.
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_B_012: A protagonist came to me, lamenting the absurdity\nof his world. Thus was a new masterpiece born!
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_B_013: Ohoho. Oh, is that right?
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_B_014: Well, as long as you're happy, that's all that matters.
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_B_015: You clearly have an eye for useful products!\nAnything else I might like?
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_B_016: As a master auteur, I'm not lacking for gold. I can\npay you handsomely!
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_B_017: Music to my ears, dear Dante. We've got plenty of\nrare items to see! Just say the word.
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_B_018: I see. Then I'll buy...productivity!
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_B_019: "Productivity"?
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_B_020: I never have enough time to write! I need a medicine\nthat would give me an extra arm or two.
MID_SE_Tal_Dan_B_021: You know, that may be the only thing I don't have\nin stock...